\par
components, then the input-output relation between (x, z) and P may not depend on all the
\par
details of the whole vector (x, z), but only on a smaller number of values that can be
\par
calculated from (x, z). The technique of "nondimensionalization" (Lin and Segel, 1988, p.
\par
198) reduces the number of parameters and variables in a model to a minimum by re-
\par
expressing its equations in terms of dimensionless algebraic combinations of the original\copyright{} COX ASSOCIATES, 1999. 503 Franklin St., Denver, CO, 80218. Ph 303-388-1778; Fax --303-388-0609. tony@cox-associates.com
\par
