Geoengineering
\par
If abatement is considered too costly, other options
\par
may be contemplated to limit climate change. One
\par
approach is to engineer the biogeochemical system,
\par
either to alter the rate of carbon sequestration, or to
\par
increase planetary albedo. 11 The former can be put
\par
into practice through strategies such as planting
\par
trees, or perhaps seeding the oceans. 12 The latter are
\par
typified by the injection of sulphates into the strato-
\par
sphere, and lofting of solar sails into earth orbit. In
