PARAMETERS
\par
The correlation structure among POD growth rates
\par
at a single time, and for single PODs over time, may be
\par
complex. Both substitution and complementarities are
\par
observed among specific PODs in certain applications.
\par
For example, either CFC-11 or 12 can be used as a
\par
refrigerant in some applications, and each can be used
\par
to produce similar foam products. In household refrig-
\par
erators, the compounds are complementary: CFC-12 is
\par
used as the refrigerant and CFC-11 is used in the foam
\par
insulation. Similarly, methyl chloroform and CFC-113
\par
are substitutes in some solvent applications, but their use
\par
may be positively correlated because both are subject to
\par
the same waste-disposal regulations. Fully specifying these
\par
relationships would entail a level of detail not warranted
