\par
Let us now consider how an expert system can use decision theory to recommend features
\par
for observation to narrow a differential diagnosis. First, the system enumerates all possible
\par
observation strategies. An example of an observation strategy is
\par
Observe f3. If f3 is present, then observe f2; otherwise, make no further obser-
\par
vations and make the diagnosis. If f3 and f2 are present, then observe f7, and
\par
