Until 1990, he was an associate
\par
professor at Carnegie Mellon
\par
University. He has an M.A. from
\par
Cambridge University, an M.Des.
\par
from the Royal College of Art, and a Ph.D. from
\par
Carnegie Mellon University. His research interests
\par
are in decision theory and AI, particularly in rea-
\par
soning under uncertainty. He is the author of DEMOS,
\par
software for probabilistic modeling and uncertainty
\par
analysis. He has developed applications in energy
