\par
fall within the range given by the IPCC. However, if the
\par
late 20th-century patterns of growth in energy consump-
\par
tion within developing countries continue unconstrained,
\par
we would expect the high emission levels in Figure 3 to
\par
be possible. Even if these high rates of emissions are not
\par
reached, the projections shown in Figure 3 demonstrate
\par
the sensitivity of small differences in energy growth
\par
rates and associated carbon emissions. These projections
