\par
upper atmospheric particle layers would be to introduce
\par
large quantities of finely divided dust particles or an
\par
aerosol producing gas (SO 2) into the stratosphere. The
\par
atmospheric oxidation of SO 2, for example, provides
\par
sulfuric acid droplets. Particles present in the strato-
\par
sphere above about 15 km have a residence time of
\par
about a year, so that a haze layer could be maintained
\par
with relatively low temporal rates of addition. The injec-
\par
