\par
\textbf{civil, criminal, and administrative procedure and rules of evidence in-}
\par
\textbf{volve an effort to strike a balance between accuracy and legal costs. The}
\par
\textbf{regulation of lawyers in litigation and some other settings is appropriately}
\par
\textbf{viewed, for present purposes, as an aspect of procedural rules concerned}
\par
\textbf{with achieving accurate outcomes while not incurring excessive costs.}
\par
\textbf{Implicit judgments concerning the value of accuracy are central in assess-}
\par
\textbf{ing major legal reforms (such as substituting an inquisitorial system for}
\par
\textbf{an adversarial system), evaluating more modest changes (limiting discov-}
\par
\textbf{ery or the use of expert witnesses), determining how adjudicators should}
\par
\textbf{exercise discretion (pretrial orders concerning the conduct of litigation),}
\par
\textbf{and designing and using alternative dispute resolution (often specified by}
\par
\textbf{contract).}
\par
\textbf{Many aspects of substantive law also are concerned with accuracy.}
\par
\textbf{Most obvious are special burdens of proof in particular areas of law (such}
\par
\textbf{as burden shifting in employment discrimination cases or res ipsa loquitur}
\par
\textbf{in tort law) and rules concerning what evidence meets even conventional}
\par
\textbf{proof burdens (such as whether a dealer's complaint to a manufacturer}
\par
\textbf{is sufficient evidence of an antitrust conspiracy to reach a jury). Also}
\par
\textbf{important are components of substantive law that determine which cate-}
\par
\textbf{gories of behavior are to be distinguished. For example, when assault}
\par
\textbf{with intent to commit murder is made a crime separate from simple as-}
\par
\textbf{sault, the legal system distinguishes two types of behavior, with the result}
\par
\textbf{that sanctions are more precisely tailored to individuals' conduct. When}
\par
\textbf{various categories of consequential damages are allowed, defendants'}
\par
\textbf{payments may reflect plaintiffs' actual harm more closely; but consequen-}
\par
\textbf{tial damages sometimes are disallowed because they would be too costly}
\par
\textbf{to establish or may be so prone to error that defendants' payments would}
\par
\textbf{less accurately reflect differences in actual harm.}
\par
\textbf{This article is primarily concerned with the question of why accuracy}
\par
\textbf{is valuable. It is assumed throughout that more accuracy can be obtained}
\par
\textbf{only at a higher cost.1 No attempt is made to determine which legal rules}
\par
\textbf{are more accurate, by how much, and at what cost. Such inquiries are}
\par
\textbf{best made case by case. Rather, the analysis seeks to illuminate the}
\par
\textbf{following sort of inquiry: if a contemplated legal reform would increase}
\par
\textbf{accuracy in some specified manner and increase cost by a determined}
\par
\textbf{amount, is the reform desirable?}
\par
\textbf{' Some changes in the legal system might make it simultaneously more accurate and}
\par
\textbf{cheaper, but it is usually obvious that such changes are desirable (from the economic}
\par
\textbf{perspective employed here) and thus analytically uninteresting to consider them.ACCURACY IN ADJUDICATION 309}
\par
\textbf{Other closely related questions are considered as well. In particular,}
\par
\textbf{this article addresses how the cost of improving accuracy depends on}
\par
\textbf{other aspects of the legal system (such as the extent to which a law is}
\par
\textbf{enforced) and how problems of accuracy affect the appropriate design of}
\par
\textbf{other elements of the system (such as whether sanctions should be higher}
\par
\textbf{or lower when inaccuracy is a more serious problem). The analysis also}
\par
\textbf{examines expenditures on legal advice, in particular whether private par-}
\par
\textbf{ties' incentives to seek advice when contemplating how to behave or}
\par
\textbf{when litigating are socially appropriate. (For example, do parties tend to}
\par
\textbf{spend too much or too little to pursue their interests in adjudication?)}
\par
\textbf{Largely separate discussions will be offered for three important legal}
\par
\textbf{contexts-the determination of damages, of liability, and of future rights}
\par
\textbf{and obligations-because the analysis differs substantially for each. Part}
\par
\textbf{II examines a scenario in which different acts cause different levels of}
\par
\textbf{harm. While the average level of damage is known, or can be ascertained}
\par
\textbf{at low cost, the particular level of damages in a given case can be deter-}
\par
\textbf{mined only after more substantial expenditures are made. The question}
\par
\textbf{is whether it is worth the cost to measure damages more accurately.}
\par
\textbf{Accurate damage determination may improve individuals' incentives}
\par
\textbf{to behave properly.2 If I contemplate committing an act that is unusually}
\par
\textbf{harmful, I will be more careful or more likely to refrain from the act if I}
\par
\textbf{will be held responsible for the true, higher level of harm, rather than for}
\par
\textbf{the lower, average level of harm for the class of acts. (Similarly, if my}
\par
\textbf{act is less harmful than is usual, holding me liable for an accordingly low}
\par
\textbf{amount will prevent excessive deterrence of my activity or avoid creating}
\par
\textbf{excessive incentives to be cautious.) In contrast, if at the time I act I am}
\par
\textbf{unaware whether my act will cause an atypically high or low level of}
\par
\textbf{harm, knowledge that an adjudicator will determine harm precisely ex}
\par
\textbf{post will not cause me to adjust my behavior accordingly. (If my act}
\par
\textbf{creates a risk of injuring a pedestrian and I have no way of knowing how}
\par
\textbf{serious a particular injury will be, making the damages I must pay depend}
\par
\textbf{precisely on the details of the actual injury cannot affect how carefully I}
\par
\textbf{act.) Thus, greater accuracy is valuable only to the extent it involves}
\par
\textbf{dimensions about which individuals are informed at the time they act.}
\par
\textbf{Relatedly, Part II explores how greater accuracy in adjudication influ-}
\par
\textbf{ences individuals' incentives to become better informed before acting.}
\par
\textbf{Finally, Part II considers whether parties' incentives to present infor-}
