\par
\textbf{sumption that damage awards will be accurate with regard to the type of}
\par
\textbf{information they might acquire. It remains the case that such accuracy}
\par
\textbf{will be desirable only when the benefits from improved behavior exceed}
\par
\textbf{the ex ante costs of information acquisition plus the ex post costs of}
\par
\textbf{greater accuracy. That private incentives are correct establishes only that}
\par
\textbf{the benefits from improved behavior exceed the ex ante information}
