\par
\textbf{fore, plaintiffs will bear risk when results are inaccurate, but not when}
\par
\textbf{they are accurate.}
\par
\textbf{Thus, taking risk aversion into account could make accuracy more or}
\par
\textbf{less desirable than otherwise, depending on whether plaintiffs' or defen-}
\par
\textbf{dants' risk aversion were more significant. Of course, all these conclu-}
\par
\textbf{sions are mitigated to the extent parties are insured.35}
