\textbf{V. OTHER VALUES OF ACCURACY}
\par
\textbf{This article presents an economic analysis of the value of accuracy in}
\par
\textbf{adjudication. The primary focus throughout is on how accuracy affects}
\par
\textbf{the central instrumental purposes of the law. Therefore, Parts II and III,}
\par
\textbf{which discuss accuracy in determining damages and liability, emphasize}
\par
\textbf{how accuracy is relevant to the effectiveness of the law in controlling}
\par
\textbf{behavior. Part IV, on accuracy in establishing future rights and obliga-}
\par
\textbf{tions, concerns the extent to which the law's purposes in directing future}
\par
\textbf{events are fulfilled. The analysis also emphasizes costs of achieving the}
\par
\textbf{law's objectives-in particular, administrative costs and social costs aris-}
\par
\textbf{ing from the imposition of sanctions.}
\par
\textbf{Yet, much concern expressed about the accuracy of the legal system}
\par
\textbf{appears to be addressed to different objectives. Thus, accuracy may be}
\par
\textbf{valued because it advances fairness and justice, one cares about mistak-}
\par
\textbf{enly sanctioning the innocent per se, it is important to the system's legiti-}
\par
\textbf{macy that adjudication appears to be as accurate as possible, or abuse}
\par
\textbf{of power is made more difficult. Also, some procedures that affect the}
\par
\textbf{accuracy of adjudication may be valued in themselves, perhaps because}
\par
\textbf{they enhance individuals' participation in processes that will affect their}
\par
\textbf{lives.}
\par
\textbf{While there is much that has been and could be said about these issues,}
\par
\textbf{little attempt will be made to address them here. First, in most instances,}
\par
\textbf{the nature of the value at stake is not very well defined, and its grounding}
\par
\textbf{is uncertain.225 This makes application in concrete contexts and evalua-}
\par
\textbf{tion of trade-offs quite difficult. Second, the type of analysis that would}
\par
\textbf{be appropriate may be rather different from that offered here, so it seems}
\par
\textbf{useful to undertake further explorations separately.}
\par
\textbf{Nonetheless, the analysis in Parts II-IV offers some illumination of}
\par
\textbf{many of these other values. This part notes some respects in which these}
\par
\textbf{seemingly different values may be implicitly included in the economic}
\par
\textbf{analysis. It also indicates how the economic analysis may illuminate the}
\par
\textbf{extent to which other values are implicated in the contexts that have}
\par
\textbf{been examined here. These remarks will not be comprehensive. Nor can}
\par
\textbf{they be definitive with respect to the topics addressed because many of}
\par
\textbf{these values can be articulated in so many ways that an argument relevant}
\par
\textbf{to one version may be inapplicable to another.}
\par
\textbf{225 For example, Mashaw refers to his own statement of the dignitary values of due}
\par
\textbf{process as follows: "The values that fit our intuitions are vague at the margins and poten-}
\par
\textbf{tially contradictory at the core." See Mashaw, supra note 195, at 899.ACCURACY IN ADJUDICATION 383}
