The overwhelming majority of them were part-
\par
time students with full-time employment in busi-
\par
ness. They were required to participate as part of
\par
the course as announced by the lecturer in charge.
\par
There were \emph{winner4akes-all }monetary incentives
\par
of A\$50 for each experimental treatment. Casual
\par
observation of students indicated that the incen-
\par
