accounting, and plea for better accountability and greater "auditor independence".
\par
The inflationary tendencies (in America and some other countries) during the
\par
1970s boosted interest in current value and general price-level adjustments ( cf.,
\par
Gynther 1970; Ross 1969; Bedford and McKeown 1972; Hanna 1972; Rosen
\par
1972; Moonitz 1973; Revsine 1973; Revsine and Weygandt 1974; Basu and Hanna
\par
1975; van Seventer 1975, for the approach in the Netherlands; Coenenberg and
\par
Macharzina 1976; Bromwich 1977; Bromwich 1977; Davidson and Wei! 1978,
\par
Falk 1978, and many others). For a historical survey and anthology of price-level
\par
accounting (including some English publications by Fritz Schmidt) between the
