two World Wars, see Zeff ( 1976). In this context Sterling ( 1979) might be
\par
mentioned, but his book not only deals with valuation and measurement problems,
\par
it also claims that "the primary problem of accounting is that our figures do not
\par
have empirical referents" (p. 213\textbraceright -the latter issue became particularly prominent
