\par
free interest charge on beginning equity). 13 Above all, they analyze the distinction
\par
between \emph{unbiased }and \emph{conservative }accounting (the latter is taken to lead, in time
\par
and on average, to a firm's market price larger than its book value; i.e., their
\par
definition of "conservative accounting" is somewhat narrower than usually
\par
encountered). 14 The valuation function in unbiased as well as conservative
\par
accounting varies only insofar as the latter requires some adjustment for the
\par
understating of operating assets-this may reflect the important distinction in
\par
reporting operating versus financing activities.
