\par
Suppose when I go home at night, I want to know if my family
\par
is home before I try the doors. (Perhaps the most convenient
\par
door to enter is double locked when nobody is home.) Now,
\par
often when my wife leaves the house, she turns on an outdoor
\par
light. However, she sometimes turns on this light if she is ex-
\par
pecting a guest. Also, we have a dog. When nobody is home,
\par
the dog is put in the backyard. The same is true if the dog has
\par
bowel troubles. Finally, if the dog is in the backyard, I will
\par
probably hear her barking (or what I think is her barking),
\par
but sometimes I can be confused by other dogs barking (Char-
\par
niak 1991).
\par
The translation of this story into a BN is straightfor-
\par
