\par
are captured in the network of Figure 2. Furthermore,
\par
the story itself implies that all variables are binary (i.e.,
\par
true or false), and Charniak developed probability dis-
\par
tributions that describe his beliefs about the prior and
\par
conditional probabilities of each event.
\par
To appreciate the illustrative power of Figure 2, note
\par
that in many ways, the absence of an arc between two
\par
nodes is more significant than the presence of an arc.
\par
An arc indicates that there is a direct relationship be-
\par
