A brief note about the form of the propositions is war-
\par
ranted. Theoretical arguments in this paper highlight the
\par
efficient form associated with individual or team entre-
\par
preneurial resources. The logic behind the propositions
\par
assumes that this efficient form will generally be observed
\par
in a population of firms, either because an individual uses
\par
foresight in laying down the initial organizational form
\par
or because processes of adaptation and/or market selec-
\par
tion forces move inefficient forms toward efficiency. In
\par
addition, a ceteris paribus assumption is not used in stat-
\par
