\par
3.2.5. The Team Entrepreneurial Form. A different
\par
organization is expected to emerge when entrepreneurial
\par
resources are spread across a large team of individuals.
\par
The following discussion is divided by different organi-
\par
zational features.
\par
The decision process. As with individual entrepre-
\par
neurs, team entrepreneurs will initiate and ratify decisions
\par
and monitor this process. However, these steps in the de-
\par
cision process may be separated and dispersed among
\par
various team entrepreneurs, such that the initiation step
\par
might be performed by one subgroup, the ratification step
\par
by another, and the monitoring step by a third.
\par
The reasons for this are multifold. The specific re-
\par
sources possessed by the various team entrepreneurs may
\par
differ, such that some entrepreneurs with greater endow-
\par
ments of creativity and alertness than of intuition and
\par
foresight are better suited to decision initiation. Other en-
\par
trepreneurs with more intuition and foresight than crea-
\par
tivity and alertness are better suited to decision ratifica-
\par
tion. In addition, decision initiation and ratification may
\par
be dispersed throughout the organization in a manner
\par
consistent with the specialization of entrepreneurial re-
\par
sources. As noted earlier, entrepreneurial resources might
\par
be of a general nature or somewhat specialized to a spe-
\par
cific problem type, such as creativity that is most valuable
\par
to the product design process. With team entrepreneur-
\par
ship, specialization of entrepreneurial resources to spe-
\par
cific tasks is more likely to emerge. Thus, an individual's
\par
entrepreneurial resources may become specialized to a
\par
specific task, such that these resources facilitate the ini-
\par
tiation and ratification of proposals for this task.
\par
Thus, I expect that:
\par
PROPOSITION 4. With team entrepreneurial re-
\par
sources, decision initiation, ratification, and monitoring
\par
will be performed by the team of individuals holding en-
\par
trepreneurial resources.
\par
PROPOSITION 5. With team entrepreneurial re-
\par
sources, decision initiation, ratification, and monitoring
\par
will be distributed among different individuals possessing
\par
different types of entrepreneurial resources.
\par
Organizational structure. One general effect of the
\par
dispersion of decision initiation and ratification steps is
\par
that monitoring takes on a significance lacking in the in-
\par
dividual entrepreneurial form. Unlike the individual en-
\par
trepreneurial form, agency costs here cannot be mini-
\par
mized by assigning the residual risk to the possessors of
\par
team entrepreneurial resources because of shirking.
\par
"Shirking" means that not all entrepreneurs will perform
\par
to the level at which their marginal rate of substitution
\par
between leisure and the production of real output is
\par
equated to their marginal rate of substitution in consump-
\par
tion (Alchian and Demsetz 1972). The present definition
\par
of entrepreneurial resources does not necessarily lead to
\par
the conclusion that shirking refers to a lower total level
\par
of utilization of entrepreneurial resources because indi-
\par
viduals with propensities to spend time engaged in the
\par
