\par
leading" expert testimony. In the absence of any other social inter-
\par
est in the particular outcome, the parties' decisions also would be
\par
efficient from a social point of view.
\par
Given these conditions, it is difficult to understand quite what
\par
is meant by the criticism that expert testimony is sometimes "mis-
