\par
As against all of these powerful forces tending toward increased
\par
investment in litigation expenditure, the evidentiary standard for
\par
the admissibility of scientific evidence can have only a limited
\par
marginal effect."8 The problem with the Frye standard and its sug-
\par
gested variants is that its marginal effect is in the wrong direction-
\par
toward reinforcing rather than dampening all of the other influ-
\par
