\par
igational aids, so long as they all qualify under some generic stan-
\par
dard as "scientific" methods. At a more profound level, Daubert
\par
also could be read as questioning whether Polaris exists at all or,
\par
even if it does, whether its location is important or even useful to
\par
the adjudicatory enterprise.
