Sec. 2. However, we believe that there is a plausible
\par
explanation for this result.
\par
There are actually two policies that are optimized
\par
in the CETA-R model-these are the carbon emissions
\par
policy and the investment policy. The optimal invest-
\par
ment policy is relatively insensitive to most parameter
\par
variations (hence the focus on sensitivity of carbon
\par
emissions and carbon shadow prices in Sec. 2). How-
\par
ever, variations in the utility discount rate do affect the
\par
optimal investment policy (not surprisingly). Conse-
\par
quently, to understand the relative benefits of resolving
\par
