\par
D\&Rs. Given that the solution improves from one D\&R to the next,
\par
more iterations are required to significantly improve the
\par
solutions provided to the last D\&Rs.
\par
(c) \emph{Tabu list}. The tabu list has length \emph{T} and its positions are indexed
\par
from 0 to \emph{T }-1. Each solution is associated with a position in the
\par
list. This position is the objective value of the solution modulo \emph{T}
\par
and the value stored at this place is the iteration number at
\par
which the solution will loose its tabu status. When a neighboring
\par
