\par
value modulo \emph{T }provides its position in the tabu list. If the value
\par
found at this position is greater than the current iteration
\par
number then the move is tabu, otherwise it is accepted. Clearly,
\par
this approach can filter out legitimate solutions. For example, two
\par
solutions will collide at the same position within the list if their
\par
objective values differ by a multiple of \emph{T }. However, \emph{T }is set to a
\par
large value, so that such an occurrence is unlikely. The tabu
\par
tenure is equal to the number of iterations divided by 2.
\par
It is worth noting that the objective value is an integer because
\par
