3.4. I m p l e m e n t a t i o n
\par
Similar to many other fields, recent years have seen
\par
a boom of released application software for Bayesian
\par
decision analysis. The examples in Table 2 were selec-
\par
ted to represent the three dominant approaches to
\par
Bayesian decision analysis: decision trees, influence
\par
diagrams, and belief networks. Apparently, the present
\par
trend is to provide an easy compatibility with spread-
\par
sheet programs. In fact, the progress in spreadsheets
\par
tends to bring more and more of such computation
\par
directly in spreadsheets.
\par
