\par
Keywords: Bayesian statistics; Decision analysis; Environment; Fisheries; Natural resources; Risk analysis; Uncertainty; Water
\par
1. Introduction
\par
Starting with an unconventional approach re-
\par
quires time, imagination, and ability to find
\par
analogies. This is our experience from applied
\par
sciences, when trying to digest and apply compu-
\par
tational approaches so that they would benefit us
\par
in solving real problems. The methodological lit-
\par
erature is blooming with most interesting ideas
\par
and techniques, yet the way to applications tends
\par
to be long and hard, albeit a most interesting one,
\par
