\par
2 .6 . Case 5: Cod fisheries management
\par
In fisheries management, the relationship be-
\par
tween the adult spawning stock and the number
\par
of recruits obtained is an essential problem. This
\par
relationship can be modelled in a number of
\par
ways and several competing models exist. More-
\par
over, the unstable environmental factors often
\par
increase the level of uncertainty and complicate
\par
the analysis of historical data.
\par
Therefore, several alternative hypotheses and
\par
models should be tested in a decision analysis
\par
context in order to see, which assumptions really
\par
matter from the management point of view. It is
\par
natural, that the simulation results obtained by
\par
various models differ, but this does not mean
\par
that the recommended action should differ.
\par
Kuikka et al. (1999) analyzed the Baltic cod
\par
fisheries management by an influence diagram
\par
model. The conditional probability distributions
\par
(obtained as a result of 300 Monte Carlo simu-
\par
lations with different recruitment models and de-
\par
cision alternatives), were combined by using the
\par
influence diagram model as a meta-model.
\par
In this type of approach, it is important to
\par
note that the final uncertainty estimate of the
\par
three combined models is very dependent on the
\par
probability (weight) given to each of the models,
\par
not much on the parameter uncertainty of a sin-
\par
gle model. However, it is very difficult to justify
\par
certain probabilities for single models, because
\par
there are several justified assumptions about the
\par
future development of environmental factors in
\par
the Baltic Sea. As a result, the final uncertainty
\par
estimate is a very subjective one.
\par
In this analysis the value-of-information anal-
\par
ysis showed, that the information robustness of
\par
the management system can be improved by us-
\par
ing a bigger mesh size in the trawl fishery. By
\par
this strategic decision, it was possible to have an
\par
effect on the tactical decision making, which is
\par
based on total allowable catches. In other
\par
words, if some part of the population's mortality
\par
control is based on a large mesh size, the con-
\par
trol based on quota system is not that important
\par
anymore in the overall control of mortality.
