\textbf{Four more subjects were discarded because there was}
\par
\textbf{no value X4 that would make them indifferent in the last}
\par
\textbf{question. This is a consequence of the boundedness of}
\par
\textbf{the life-duration variable and the time spans we chose.}
\par
\textbf{We could have avoided the nonexistence of X4 by using}
\par
\textbf{smaller time spans. It is well-known, however, that util-}
\par
\textbf{ity is almost linear over small intervals. Hence, for cur-}
\par
\textbf{vature of utility to be nonnegligible, the replies should}
\par
\textbf{cover a significant part of the subjects' (mostly aged}
\par
\textbf{around 25) envisioned life duration, which explains}
\par
\textbf{why no smaller time spans were used. Ultimately, then,}
\par
\textbf{the responses of 41 subjects were retained for further}
\par
\textbf{analysis in the life-duration experiment.}
