\textbf{3.4. Discussion of Results}
\par
\textbf{Summary of Findings. Our experiments have con-}
\par
\textbf{firmed the general finding of diminishing marginal util-}
\par
\textbf{ity both for life years and for money. The TO elicitations}
\par
\textbf{suggest that the outcomes chosen in our experiments,}
\par
\textbf{coincidentally, exhibit similar curvature of utility for life}
\par
\textbf{duration as for money. Whereas under EU, the CE and}
\par
\textbf{PE elicitations should yield the same utilities as the TO}
\par
\textbf{elicitations, the observed CE elicitations suggest more}
\par
\textbf{concavity of utility than the TO elicitations, and the PE}
\par
\textbf{elicitations in turn suggest more concavity than the CE}
\par
\textbf{elicitations. In the monetary experiment, the differences}
\par
\textbf{between the CE elicitations and the TO elicitations are}
\par
\textbf{not significant and thus do not imply rejection of EU. In}
\par
\textbf{the life-duration experiment, the CE utilities do suggest}
\par
\textbf{significantly more risk aversion than the TO utilities. In}
\par
\textbf{both experiments, the PE utilities suggest more risk}
\par
\textbf{aversion than the CE utilities. PE utilities also suggest}
\par
\textbf{more risk aversion than TO utilities in the monetary}
