\par
from past data. For example, it may be possible to infer that
\par
a high sales value was because of an advertising campaign.
\par
This would have benefits not only in forecasting, but also in
\par
assessing the effectiveness of marketing.\emph{R. Webby, M. O'Connor / International Journal of Forecasting 12 (1996) 91-118 }sition of special events. Such an approach may
\par
facilitate the interpretation of 'soft' event in-
\par
formation by the judgemental forecaster, and
\par
have broader implications for the integration of
\par
soft and hard information in general decision
\par
making.
