\textbf{Biographies: }Richard WEBBY is a lecturer in the School of
\par
Information Systems at the University of New South Wales.
\par
His research focuses on the development and empirical
\par
validation of software designed to support human judgement.
\par
His doctoral work examined the application of a forecasting
\par
support system to aid judgemental forecasters with both time
\par
series data and extra-model information.
\par
Marcus O'CONNOR is a member of the academic staff of
\par
the School of Information Systems at the University of New
\par
South Wales. His research interests centre on the way people
\par
use information in making judgements. He typically uses the
\par
forecasting task as a vehicle to examine the ability of people
\par
to combine both causal and non-causal information in making
\par
forecasts.
