Keen recognized this gap in MIS theory in his 1980 ICIS paper when he wrote,
\par
``There is no clear theoretical base [for MIS] and no match between theory and
\par
method'' [31]. Ten years later he remarked that, ``Organizations continue to spend
\par
money on information systems without a link to the value of the system and MIS
\par
